By John Brodie at 11:13am, Feb03,05
AMENDMENT NUMBER6TO CONTRACT NO.2985BETWEEN
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, AND THE CITY OF CHEYENNE-LARAMIE
COUNTY JOINT POWERS BOARD
1.Parties.The parties to this Amendment are the City of Cheyenne, amunicipal corporation, duly
organized and existing under thelawsof the State of Wyoming, whose principal address is2101
O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne Wyoming 82001,“City”, and the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming-
Laramie County Joint Powers Board, a statutorily authorized entity organized and existing under
laws of the State of Wyoming, whose address is P.O.Box 2477, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001,
"JPB".
2.
Purpose of Amendment.The purpose of this amendment is to amend Paragraph number 7of the
Lease Agreement between the parties dated March 9,1992 as follows:
“All sanitation, water and sewer service will be paid for by the JPB.TheJPB's annual cost of
water will be as follows:
a.Upon the 1992Lease Agreement #2985 being amended and signed by all parties, The JPB
agrees to pay 50% of allmetered water consumption on J PB leased facilities through
December 31,2025.
b.Beginning January 1,2026JPB agrees to pay for100% of all metered water consumption on
JPBleased facilities.
The cost of all metered water consumption will be at the most current approved water rate.
3.Other Terms and Conditions Remain Unchanged.All other terms and conditions of the
original Lease remain unchanged and infullforce and effect except as modified by previous
amendments.
4.Siguatures.In witness thereof, the parties to this Amendment, through their duly authorized
representatives, have executed this Amendment on the dates set out below and certify that they
have read, understood and agreed to the terms and conditions of this Amendment.
The effective date of this Amendment is
,2025.
