Dear Tom,
I want to thankyou Jeannie and Mike again personally for meeting with our team on January905todiscuss
Cheyenne Frontier Days(CFD)water consumption andbilling.Aswe discussed the Boardof Public Utilities(BOPU)
has big challenges ahead with wat e shortages due to posible Colorado River cut ailment con serva ton and declining
water sales revenue, as well as the expense to maintain a very sophisticated extensive raw water collection and potable
distribution system.We understand the reasons behind theoriginal1992Lease Agreement and the efforts to aid CFD
with zero or reduced annual water fees, unfortunately the BOP U cannot sustain those commitments in our current water
and financial climate.
We appreciate your understanding of our situation and the need to have CFD pay for all of their metered water
consumption on CFD leased facilities.Aswe discussed on the9in our meeting, both parties agreed to the following
payment schedule for metered water consumption moving forward:
1.Upon the1992Lease Agreement #2985 being amended and signed by all parties, CFD agrees to pay 50% of all
metered water consumption onCFD leased facilities through December31,2025.
2.
Beginning January 1, 2026 CFD agrees to pay for 100% of all metered water consumption on CFD leased
facilities.
As we discussed at ourmeeting on the 9u, I would request you send a confirmation response letter tome at your earliest
convenience approving the above payment schedule andwewill begin the process to amend the1992Lease Agreement
with helpfrom the Cityof Cheyenne.
Thanks againfor your willingness and cooperation tomeetwith us and agree to thesefuture conditions for the payment of
water consumption on CFD leased facilities.If you have any questions or concerms about this letter, please feel free to
contact me at your convenience at 307-637-6464.
